# The compose build context is the repo root, so everything here would be sent
# to the daemon on every `make run` -- including the 237 MB legacy client tree,
# which no stage copies and nothing in the app reads.
#
# server/css and server/js are build INPUTS. Their outputs -- app.css and the
# editor bundle -- are committed under server/public, which is a different path
# and stays in; the Go build reads neither source directory. Everything the
# image needs is already generated before docker starts, which is why no stage
# runs npm, esbuild, Tailwind, templ or sqlc.
#
# .env files never belong in a build context, even when no stage copies one into
# the final image: anything sent to the daemon is readable from the build cache.
.git
client
node_modules
build
db
server/css
server/js
**/.env
